    {
      "id": "interval-recognition",
      "title": "Interval Recognition",
      "level": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "**Track:** ear-training | **Difficulty:** 3/10 | **Time:** ~10 min"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Hearing intervals accurately is the foundation of sight-singing, transcription, and harmonising by ear."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "consonant-intervals",
      "title": "Consonant intervals",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Unison, P4, P5, P8 — stable. Major and minor 3rds and 6ths — sweet. Learn these first."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dissonant-intervals",
      "title": "Dissonant intervals",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "m2, M2, m7, M7, tritone — tense. Identify by tension level and melodic direction."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "reference-songs",
      "title": "Reference songs",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "M2 = *Happy Birthday* first two notes. m3 = *Greensleeves* start. M3 = *When the Saints*. P4 = *Here Comes the Bride*. P5 = *Star Wars* fanfare. M6 = *My Bonnie*. m7 = *Star Trek* opening (partial)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "practice",
      "title": "Practice",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Use apps (Functional Ear Trainer, Complete Ear Trainer). Sing intervals up and down from any note. Partner testing: one plays, one names."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
